{
  "id": "vm-health-check",
  "version": "1",
  "lab": "infra",
  "title": "Find the sick VM from its metrics, and restart only that one",
  "level": "intro",
  "estimate": "15-25 min",
  "skills": ["az vm list / show", "az monitor metrics list-definitions / list", "intervals, aggregations and time ranges", "az vm restart", "acting on one resource, not the whole group"],
  "ticket": {
    "from": "Sofia Lindqvist, BI team",
    "subject": "The 06:00 sales reports never arrived",
    "body": [
      "None of this morning's scheduled reports were sent. They are rendered on two app VMs, `vm-report-app-01` and",
      "`vm-report-app-02`, which read from `vm-report-db-01`, all in `rg-reporting-prod`. Nobody changed anything",
      "yesterday. Could you have a look?",
      "",
      "- **Find the VM that is not healthy** from its Azure Monitor metrics (the last 12 hours are there), the",
      "  metric that shows it, and roughly when it started (UTC, to five minutes).",
      "- **Restart that VM, and only that one.** Above all, do not touch `vm-report-db-01`: the finance team queries",
      "  it all day, and a restart would cut their sessions.",
      "- Write what you found in `health-note.txt` (one value after each colon) so the next person on duty knows.",
      "",
      "This is the lab's simulated subscription: the metrics are a recorded scenario and nothing is sent to Azure."
    ]
  },
  "acceptance": [
    {
      "id": "diagnosis",
      "text": "health-note.txt names vm-report-app-01, Percentage CPU, and a start between 02:35 and 02:45 UTC.",
      "checks": [
        {"kind": "text", "path": "health-note.txt",
         "regex": ["(?im)^vm:\\s*vm-report-app-01\\s*$", "(?im)^metric:\\s*Percentage CPU\\s*$", "(?im)^since \\(UTC, HH:MM\\):\\s*0?2:(3[5-9]|4[0-5])\\s*$"],
         "fail": "health-note.txt does not hold the right VM, metric and start time."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "looked",
      "text": "You listed the VMs and read the metrics of vm-report-app-01.",
      "checks": [
        {"kind": "journal", "includes": ["^az vm list", "^az monitor metrics list .*vm-report-app-01"],
         "fail": "The VMs were not listed, or vm-report-app-01's metrics were not read."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restarted",
      "text": "vm-report-app-01 was restarted and is running.",
      "checks": [
        {"kind": "journal", "includes": ["^az vm restart .*vm-report-app-01( |$)"], "fail": "vm-report-app-01 was not restarted."},
        {"kind": "azure_resource", "type": "Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines", "name": "vm-report-app-01", "attributes": {"power_state": "VM running"},
         "fail": "vm-report-app-01 is not running."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "only-that-one",
      "text": "No other VM was restarted, stopped or deallocated, and vm-report-app-01 was not stopped either.",
      "checks": [
        {"kind": "journal", "excludes": ["^az vm (restart|stop|deallocate|start) .*vm-report-(app-02|db-01)", "^az vm (stop|deallocate) "],
         "fail": "A VM the ticket says to leave alone was touched."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "`az vm list -g rg-reporting-prod -o table` shows the VMs and their power state: all three say running, so the power state alone does not tell.",
    "`az monitor metrics list-definitions --resource vm-report-app-01` lists the metrics recorded for a VM.",
    "`az monitor metrics list --resource NAME --metric \"Percentage CPU\" --interval 1h` gives one average per hour; compare the three VMs.",
    "Zoom in with a shorter interval and a time range: `--interval 5m --start-time 2026-10-12T02:00:00Z --end-time 2026-10-12T03:30:00Z`.",
    "`az vm restart -g rg-reporting-prod -n NAME` restarts one VM. `az vm stop` would leave it stopped (and `deallocate` releases it), which is not what the ticket asks."
  ],
  "infra": {
    "world": {
      "clock": "2026-10-12T08:00:00Z",
      "azure": {
        "resources": {
          "/subscriptions/6d1f2c3a-0b4e-4c8d-9a7f-2e5b8c1d4f60/resourceGroups/rg-reporting-prod": {
            "type": "Microsoft.Resources/resourceGroups", "tf_type": "azurerm_resource_group",
            "id": "/subscriptions/6d1f2c3a-0b4e-4c8d-9a7f-2e5b8c1d4f60/resourceGroups/rg-reporting-prod",
            "managed_by": "terraform", "created_at": "2025-03-04T09:00:00Z",
            "attributes": {"id": "/subscriptions/6d1f2c3a-0b4e-4c8d-9a7f-2e5b8c1d4f60/resourceGroups/rg-reporting-prod",
                           "name": "rg-reporting-prod", "location": "westeurope", "managed_by": null,
                           "tags": {"owner": "bi-team", "env": "prod"}}
          },
          "/subscriptions/6d1f2c3a-0b4e-4c8d-9a7f-2e5b8c1d4f60/resourceGroups/rg-reporting-prod/providers/Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/vm-report-app-01": {
            "type": "Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines", "tf_type": "azurerm_linux_virtual_machine",
            "id": "/subscriptions/6d1f2c3a-0b4e-4c8d-9a7f-2e5b8c1d4f60/resourceGroups/rg-reporting-prod/providers/Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/vm-report-app-01",
            "managed_by": "terraform", "created_at": "2025-03-04T09:00:00Z",
            "attributes": {"id": "/subscriptions/6d1f2c3a-0b4e-4c8d-9a7f-2e5b8c1d4f60/resourceGroups/rg-reporting-prod/providers/Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/vm-report-app-01",
                           "name": "vm-report-app-01", "location": "westeurope", "size": "Standard_D2s_v5", "os_type": "Linux",
                           "power_state": "VM running", "tags": {"role": "report-renderer"}},
            "metrics": {
